id: sl_diag
label: SL Diagnostic
package: platform_core
description: >
  Retained diagnostics framework. Reserves a retained, non-initialized RAM
  region (.sl_diag_retained.noinit) that holds a control block, one or two
  retained record slots, an optional Summary Ring and an optional Mini
  Emergency Tail. Crash Capture and stack components capture incidents into
  this region as TLV records. Stack teams link optional providers through the
  sl_diag_linked_provider template contribution (see sl_diag_format.h).

  Diagnostic profile (SL_DIAG_PROFILE) selects which features are compiled in.
  With profile Off, no retained region is allocated and the public API is
  stubbed; RAM cost matches not having the component.

  Profiles:
    Off — no retained diagnostics.
    Crash Basic — CPU crash record (Crash Capture / CPU Crash provider).
    Crash Standard — Crash Basic plus Trigger, Reset/Boot and Build metadata.
    Crash with Summary — Crash Standard plus Summary Ring and recent-event tail.
    Full Template — all features, including non-crash capture and extended
    providers (System, heap, host interface, NWP health, and similar).

  SL_DIAG_PROFILE — Diagnostic profile. Controls SL_DIAG_ENABLE, retained layout
  size, Summary Ring, non-crash triggers, extended providers, and repeat
  counting. Default: Off.

  SL_DIAG_SLOT_COUNT — Number of retained record slots (1 or 2). Two slots
  enable copy-on-commit so a new capture can be written while the previous
  record remains readable until commit completes. Default: 1.

  SL_DIAG_EMERGENCY_ENABLE — When enabled, reserves a Mini Emergency Tail with
  minimal crash evidence if a full record commit does not finish before reset.
  Default: disabled.

  SL_DIAG_STACK_SNAPSHOT_BYTES — Optional raw stack bytes copied into the CPU
  crash scratch and CPU Crash TLV (0 disables). Must be a multiple of 4; range
  0–256. Increases fault-handler scratch and every record slot size. Default: 0.

  SL_DIAG_CAPTURE_TIME_BUDGET_US — Provider capture time budget in microseconds
  for hard fault, assert, and non-crash triggers (IPC timeout, manual capture,
  and similar). Only provider callbacks consume this budget; core TLVs and
  commit are not charged. Crash paths run with interrupts masked while the
  hardware watchdog may still run. Range 1–5000; reference default 5000.

  SL_DIAG_MAX_PRIVACY_CLASS — Highest provider privacy class executed in this
  build. Providers above this class are not run; their status is recorded as
  REDACTED. Values: Public, Operational (default), Sensitive, Secret. 
category: Services|Diagnostics
quality: evaluation
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
provides:
- name: sl_diag
requires:
- name: sl_core
- name: component_catalog
- name: enum
- name: status
- name: cycle_counter
- name: hal_emu
  condition: [device_has_emu]
root_path: platform_core/platform/service/sl_diag
config_file:
- path: config/sl_diag_config.h
include:
- path: inc
  file_list:
  - path: sl_diag.h
  - path: sl_diag_format.h
  - path: sl_diag_reason_ids.h
  - path: sli_diag.h
  - path: sl_diag_linked_providers_default.h
- path: src
  file_list:
  - path: sli_diag_internal.h
source:
- path: src/sl_diag.c
- path: src/sl_diag_capture_profiles.c
- path: src/sl_diag_crc.c
- path: src/sl_diag_fault.c
- path: src/sl_diag_metadata.c
- path: src/sl_diag_provider.c
- path: src/sl_diag_record.c
- path: src/sl_diag_reset_boot.c
- path: src/sl_diag_summary_ring.c
- path: src/sl_diag_writer.c
template_file:
- path: config/template/sl_diag_linked_providers_autogen.h.jinja
  export: true
template_contribution:
- name: event_handler
  value:
    event: platform_init
    include: sli_diag.h
    handler: sli_diag_platform_init
  priority: -9990
- name: event_handler
  value:
    event: service_init
    include: sli_diag.h
    handler: sli_diag_service_init
  priority: 9000
- name: component_catalog
  value: sl_diag
- name: sl_diag_enable
  value: 1
